rtifacts/clued-validation/information-flow-m0d/599f24be25fb/run-results.json":"f97ac94c2407ced7c034ad8cf0d854a19da7f8c22300a2664f75e4000267bcc6","artifacts/clued-validation/information-flow-m0d/599f24be25fb/run.json":"13997eb0f6dd493ffa41f4bd73aec91fbbed610ee99df69858eae77640af10f8","artifacts/clued-validation/information-flow-m0d/599f24be25fb/setup.json":"ce1cd6cfe57e21af31d2d27cd1453d83539b97e684b2611d82ecf196cfb0b7ea","artifacts/clued-validation/information-flow-m0d/599f24be25fb/review-input.json":"70d1fe8da906fdd3af000fc77a05b43b93c8da3b20e4ed22624516fadff050df"},"verdict":"HOLD_FAIL","counts":{"blocker":1,"major":0,"minor":16},"findings":[{"id":"F01","severity":"BLOCKER","file":"apps/clued-cloud/supabase/migrations/20260924190000_information_flow_promotion.sql","line":852,"one_line":"S3 redefines public.clued_user_decision_supersede with auth.uid(), removing the v12 authorization_owner_v12 direct-human guard: a delegated-OAuth JWT (client_id) can again supersede Canonical Decisions via PostgREST and /v1/decisions/supersede, which is a non-additive authority regression; information-flow-promotion-db.test.mjs:295-303 asserts it commits, and register L12 wrongly says the database guard refuses it"},{"id":"F02","severity":"MINOR","file":"artifacts/clued-validation/information-flow-m0d/599f24be25fb/reproducibility.json","line":5,"one_line":"Claim 18 cannot be verified: the second run is not committed, its digests are not recorded (only cross_check_equal booleans), and no script generates this file; this reviewer's own T1 re-run was blocked by the sandbox (PostgREST image pull 403/429)"},{"id":"F03","severity":"MINOR","file":"scripts/information-flow/m0d-seal.mjs","line":151,"one_line":"The M0D-B08 seal row is plain isolation.result=PASS with no S1-production-apply qualifier (L26/L28), though contract B08 says 'Zero production writes' unscoped and the scope limit rests on an Agent-written Decision under OPEN_BY_OD-5"},{"id":"F04","severity":"MINOR","file":"artifacts/clued-validation/information-flow-m0d/599f24be25fb/part-a/a01-parents.json","line":132,"one_line":"The M0-C node --test entry exited 1 on attempt 3 of 3; PASS_WITH_DISCLOSED_NONDETERMINISM does not literally meet A01 'each parent's own entry exits zero'; the seal /^PASS/ test lets it through, but the label is conditional on Owner acceptance"},{"id":"F05","severity":"MINOR","file":"scripts/information-flow/m0d-regression.mjs","line":222,"one_line":"The db:test:v2 failure is classified as non-environmental, while contract B07 allows only environmental baseline failures; acceptance rests on Decision item 7, which is hard-coded in the runner, and nothing proves dea0a61b/2aa51246 are on main"},{"id":"F06","severity":"MINOR","file":"apps/clued-cloud/evals/information-flow-e2e/scenarios/e2e-15.mjs","line":97,"one_line":"The E2E-15 re-pointed-Evidence promote is rejected as confirmation_view_stale (view-digest check precedes the Evidence check); the assertion accepts either code, so the promote-time observed_requires_server_computed_evidence guard is covered only at DB level"},{"id":"F07","severity":"MINOR","file":"apps/clued-cloud/evals/information-flow-e2e/isolation-guard.cjs","line":88,"one_line":"Guard ledgers are written only on exit, so the 3 SIGKILLed Worker hosts leave no allowed-connection ledger; isolation.json says processes:4 although 7 Node processes ran, and the gap is undisclosed"},{"id":"F08","severity":"MINOR","file":"apps/clued-cloud/evals/information-flow-e2e/run.mjs","line":50,"one_line":"npx wrangler --dry-run and npx supabase child processes run without the isolation-guard --require, contrary to README 'every harness Node process'; IFE2E_DENY_PORTS value is not recorded"},{"id":"F09","severity":"MINOR","file":"apps/clued-cloud/evals/information-flow-e2e/aggregate.mjs","line":150,"one_line":"Run flags (--skip-reset, --ttl-wait-ms, --only) and the actual TTL wait in ms are not recorded in run.json; --skip-reset would not be detected"},{"id":"F10","severity":"MINOR","file":"apps/clued-cloud/evals/information-flow-e2e/evidence.mjs","line":98,"one_line":"The normalized digest drops step ledgers, assertion observed values and notes, and sorts all arrays; verify-evidence computes code_tree_equal but never fails on false"},{"id":"F11","severity":"MINOR","file":"apps/clued-cloud/supabase/migrations/20260924190000_information_flow_promotion.sql","line":614,"one_line":"Token session binding uses 'is distinct from' on nullif(session_id): a JWT without a session_id claim stores NULL, making the session binding conditional"},{"id":"F12","severity":"MINOR","file":"apps/clued-cloud/supabase/migrations/20260924200000_information_flow_context_policy.sql","line":1109,"one_line":"Native token lookup has no action filter before burn: a token for one action can be burned through another action's RPC by the same user (also 20260924220000:751)"},{"id":"F13","severity":"MINOR","file":"apps/clued-cloud/evals/information-flow-e2e/scenarios/e2e-10.mjs","line":61,"one_line":"E2E-10 stripped-MTPE-key check covers only priority/action_level; other MTPE keys are not in the payload"},{"id":"F14","severity":"MINOR","file":"artifacts/clued-validation/information-flow-m0d/599f24be25fb/run-results.json","line":1,"one_line":"PASS rows in run-results.json/run.json omit the 'Agent authority confined only on the Information Flow path' qualifier (present in each scenario claims block)"},{"id":"F15","severity":"MINOR","file":"scripts/information-flow/m0d-seal.mjs","line":70,"one_line":"The A03 seal check verifies only that register IDs L01-L06 exist; it does not check content or L25/L27/L28"},{"id":"F16","severity":"MINOR","file":".github/workflows/information-flow-e2e.yml","line":117,"one_line":"actions/upload-artifact@v4 is not SHA-pinned; IFE2E_DENY_PORTS is not set in CI"},{"id":"F17","severity":"MINOR","file":"scripts/information-flow/README.md","line":26,"one_line":"README claims an earlier Node 24.19.0 M0-C run passed all 27 tests, inconsistent with contract section 2 and the observed nondeterminism; the m0d-* scripts are undocumented"}],"drive_report":null}
